      "independentTests": [],
      "dossier": {
        "summary": "Google's dated Jules changelog says the hosted service left beta on 6 August 2025, while the current Jules FAQ says it is in Public Beta. That unresolved publisher-source disagreement is preserved without adjudication. Other publisher sources describe hosted task VMs, environment setup and snapshots, plan approval, repository scope, GitHub publication, internet access, MCP connections and pull-request feedback modes; none was independently tested.",
        "releaseContext": {
          "statement": "Google's 6 August 2025 changelog is an exact dated out-of-beta milestone, not an exact backend release. The current FAQ's Public Beta label conflicts with it under potentially overlapping service applicability. The dossier therefore identifies a rolling hosted Jules service with unresolved lifecycle wording and runtime implementation.",
          "sourceId": "source-out-of-beta-2025-08-06",
          "legacySource": null
        },
        "limitations": [
          "Every behavior statement is publisher-attributed; the catalog did not start or observe a Jules task.",
          "The lifecycle disagreement is preserved as unresolved because neither source provides a correction, withdrawal or scope explanation.",
          "Dated changelog entries establish service milestones, not an immutable backend build, deployed model, VM image or task artifact.",
          "Rolling Jules documentation is not treated as exact evidence for the 2025 or 2026 milestones.",
          "No independent report with defensible service-time, repository, plan, model, tool, network and task overlap was included."
        ],
        "unknowns": [
          "Whether Jules is currently beta, post-beta, or differently labeled by region, plan, account cohort or surface.",
          "Whether Google intends the current FAQ to correct, qualify or coexist with the 6 August 2025 changelog.",
          "The backend service build, deployed code revision and change history for a particular task.",
          "The effective model, provider revision, reasoning configuration, router and fallback behavior.",
          "The task VM image digest, hardware, region, tenancy, isolation, retention and teardown behavior.",
          "The repository environment setup path, commands, dependencies, snapshot contents and restoration behavior.",
          "The effective GitHub authorization, repository, branch, organization policy and branch protections.",
          "The plan-control path, prompt context, task output route, commit identity and pull-request state.",
          "The effective internet egress controls, destinations, logging, filtering and network isolation.",
          "The enabled MCP services, tools, API keys, permissions, data destinations and autonomous side effects."
        ]
      },
